Title: claude-refresh.service fails nightly: ~/.idh missing on doudou
Created: 2026-11-18
Author: games-session

--- log ---
2026-11-18T07:59Z games-session created

--- body ---
## Context
On doudou, the user unit `~/.config/systemd/user/claude-refresh.service`
("Refresh ~/.idh (harness checkout) from git origin", `WorkingDirectory=%h/.idh`,
`ExecStart=git pull --ff-only`, fired by `claude-refresh.timer`) fails every
night with status 200/CHDIR: `~/.idh` does not exist. Last seen 2026-11-18
00:03 CET; `systemctl --user --failed` lists it. Found during a read-only
health sweep of doudou (machine project `~/CNRS/projets/actifs/doudou`).

Observation only: nothing in the harness's `scripts/` mentions
`claude-refresh` today, so the unit looks left over from an earlier
checkout layout. Cause not established.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Decide: retire the unit and timer, or point them at the current harness
      checkout.
- [ ] `systemctl --user --failed` on doudou no longer lists claude-refresh.
- [ ] If retired, the installer or a migration removes it on other machines
      that still carry it (padme?).
